; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Epicycles and Square Waves
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     fourier series, epicycles, circles, waves, animation
; SUMMARY:  Stacks spinning circles on top of each other so the tip of the last one draws a wave that gets closer and closer to a square.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A circle spins, and on its edge sits the center of a smaller
;   circle spinning three times as fast, and on that one a smaller
;   one five times as fast, and so on. The height of the last tip is
;   drawn on the right as a wave moving along. With one circle the
;   wave is a smooth sine wave. Every time round, one more circle is
;   added, and the wave gets squarer. This is the idea behind the
;   Fourier series, which builds any repeating shape out of circles,
;   and behind the "epicycles" ancient astronomers used for planets.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch. Press Stop to end. Change MOST for the largest
;   number of circles, or SPEED.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a point on a spinning circle: radius x cos, radius x sin
;   * adding circles end to end: each center is the last tip
;   * the square wave recipe: speeds 1, 3, 5, 7 ... and sizes 1, 1/3,
;     1/5, 1/7 ...
;   * keeping a history list of the last few hundred values
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use speeds 1, 2, 3, 4 ... with sizes 1, 1/2, 1/3 ... (and a minus
;     sign on every other one) for a sawtooth wave.
;   * Draw the path of the last tip too, not only its height.
;   * Use 20 circles. Do the little "ears" at the corners go away?
; ============================================================

make "most 8
make "speed 2
make "big 90            ; radius of the first circle
make "center [-220 0]
make "wavestart -40     ; where the wave begins on the screen

; Draw the chain of :n circles at angle :a, and output the last tip.
to chain :n :a
  localmake "here :center
  for [k 1 :n] [
    localmake "odd 2 * :k - 1
    localmake "r :big * 4 / (pi * :odd)
    ; the circle itself, faint
    setpencolor [190 190 210] setpensize 1
    penup setpos :here setheading 0 pendown arc 360 :r
    ; its spoke, from the center to the next center
    localmake "next list (first :here) + :r * cos :odd * :a (last :here) + :r * sin :odd * :a
    setpencolor [70 80 140] setpensize 2
    penup setpos :here pendown setpos :next
    make "here :next
  ]
  output :here
end

; The wave: newest value at the left, older values further right.
to drawwave :history
  setpencolor [220 60 80] setpensize 3
  penup
  foreach :history [
    setxy :wavestart + # - 1 ?
    pendown
  ]
  penup
end

to play
  localmake "n 1
  localmake "history []
  localmake "a 0
  forever [
    clean
    localmake "tip chain :n :a
    make "history fput last :tip :history
    if (count :history) > 420 [make "history butlast :history]
    ; a line from the tip across to the start of the wave
    setpencolor [150 150 150] setpensize 1
    penup setpos :tip pendown setxy :wavestart last :tip
    setpencolor [220 60 80] setpensize 9 penup dot :tip
    drawwave :history
    penup setxy -380 -270 setpencolor [90 90 90]
    label (sentence :n ifelse :n = 1 ["circle] ["circles])
    make "a :a + :speed
    ; after each full turn add another circle, up to MOST
    if :a >= 360 [
      make "a :a - 360
      make "n ifelse :n < :most [:n + 1] [1]
    ]
    wait 1
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 250 246]
setlabelheight 16
play
